message: "If you use this software, please cite it as below."
title: "Climate Explorer: A browser-based weather data analysis and visualisation tool"
abstract: >-
  A single-file, browser-based tool for exploring EnergyPlus Weather (.epw) files
  in 2D and 3D, built for teaching climate-responsive design to architecture
  students. Twelve views — annual heatmaps, time series, diurnal profiles,
  monthly statistics, distributions, a psychrometric chart with ASHRAE 55 comfort
  zones and Givoni–Milne passive-strategy polygons, wind roses, sun path diagrams,
  a sun path dome, an annual surface, a 3D wind rose, and a massing block casting
  the real sun shadow — arranged by five analysis modes. Psychrometrics follow the
  ASHRAE Handbook of Fundamentals; solar position follows the NOAA General Solar
  Position Calculations. The application bundles no third-party library, makes no
  network request, and ships with no weather data: the reader supplies their own
  file. The software is MIT licensed; the accompanying documentation is CC BY 4.0.
